{"ref":"character:axe-armor","lead":[{"k":"p","c":[{"i":"Animated-Alucard.gif","w":40,"h":34}]},{"k":"p","c":["DLC Content (Ode to Castlevania)"]},{"k":"p","c":["This article primarily features content only available in DLC, which may not be available in all copies of the game."]},{"k":"p","c":["The Axe Armor is a secret playable character from the Ode to Castlevania DLC of Vampire Survivors. Their starting weapon is the ",{"i":"Sprite-Axe.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:axe"}," ",{"t":"Axe","r":"weapon:axe"},"."]}],"infobox":[{"title":"Character","rows":[{"label":"Release","cells":[["31 October 2024 (Update)"]]},{"label":"Character ID","cells":[["TP_AXEARMOR"]]},{"label":"Skin ID","cells":[["DEFAULT"]]},{"label":"Controller","cells":[["TP_AxeArmor_Character"]]},{"label":"Starting weapon","cells":[[{"i":"Sprite-Axe.png","w":16,"h":16,"r":"weapon:axe"}," ",{"t":"Axe","r":"weapon:axe"}]]},{"label":"Unlocked by","cells":[["Prove to them that there is something that spins better than axes."]]},{"label":"Cost","cells":[[{"i":"Sprite-Gold_Coin.png","w":10,"h":10}," 2,000"]]},{"label":"Secret","cells":[["Yes"]]},{"label":"Ignores walls","cells":[["No"]]},{"label":"Theme","cells":[["No"]]}]},{"title":"Initial stats","rows":[{"label":"Max Health","cells":[["110"]]},{"label":"Move Speed","cells":[["+10%"]]},{"label":"Might","cells":[["+10%"]]},{"label":"Curse","cells":[["+10%"]]}]}],"sections":[{"id":"unlocking","title":"Unlocking","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":[{"i":"Sprite-Forbidden_Scrolls_of_Morbane.png","w":21,"h":21,"a":"A sprite icon representing Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane linking to Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane","r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," \"Prove to them that there is something that spins better than axes.\"\nFull unlock method hidden. Click \"Show Details\" to unhide."]},{"k":"p","c":["After obtaining the ",{"i":"Sprite-Pile_of_Secrets.png","w":20,"h":24,"r":"relic:pile-of-secrets"}," ",{"t":"Pile of Secrets","r":"relic:pile-of-secrets"},", the player must defeat 100 ",{"i":"Sprite-Axe_Armor_(enemy).png","w":13,"h":24}," Axe Armor enemies in the ",{"t":"Ode to Castlevania Stage","r":"stage:ode-to-castlevania-stage"}," with the ",{"i":"Sprite-Stellar_Blade.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:stellar-blade"}," ",{"t":"Stellar Blade","r":"weapon:stellar-blade"},", the evolution of the ",{"i":"Sprite-Discus.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:discus"}," ",{"t":"Discus","r":"weapon:discus"}," in the Cathedral area of the map. The Cathedral (the top part of the far east building) contains a room that only spawns Axe Armors. This spacious prayer room is located in the bottom-left area of the Cathedral with a pseudo-high / standing cross in the middle with a caped, praying statue at the base. There is also a ",{"i":"Sprite-Mirror_of_Truth.png","w":19,"h":24}," Mirror of Truth pickup. Doing this unlocks the Axe Armor as a playable character."]},{"k":"p","c":["Once unlocked, the Axe Armor can be purchased for ",{"i":"Sprite-Gold_Coin.png","w":10,"h":10}," 2,000, which scales with other characters purchased."]},{"k":"p","c":["Alternatively, the Axe Armor can be unlocked in the ",{"i":"Sprite-Forbidden_Scrolls_of_Morbane.png","w":16,"h":16,"r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," ",{"t":"Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane","r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," by casting the spell \"missaxalotl\"."]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"passive-bonuses","title":"Passive bonuses","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["The Axe Armor starts with +10 ",{"i":"Sprite-Max_Health.png","w":24,"h":23,"r":"powerup:max-health"}," ",{"t":"Max Health","r":"powerup:max-health"},", +10% ",{"i":"Sprite-Might.png","w":18,"h":24,"r":"powerup:might"}," ",{"t":"Might","r":"powerup:might"},", +10% ",{"i":"Sprite-Move_Speed.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"powerup:move-speed"}," ",{"t":"Move Speed","r":"powerup:move-speed"},", and +10% ",{"i":"Sprite-Curse.png","w":22,"h":24,"r":"powerup:curse"}," ",{"t":"Curse","r":"powerup:curse"},". They gain another 5% Might, 5% Move Speed and 5% Curse every 10 levels, for a max increase of +20% or +30% in total."]},{"k":"p","c":["As the description implies, they gain an additional hidden Axe every 10 levels, up to a max of 6."]},{"k":"p","c":["The Axe Armor can find special Ode to Castlevania pickups from light sources."]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"gallery","title":"Gallery","blocks":[{"k":"gallery","items":[{"i":"Sprite-Axe_Armor.png","w":84,"h":120,"c":["Axe Armor's sprite"]},{"i":"Animated-Axe_Armor.gif","w":68,"h":120,"c":["Movement animation"]},{"i":"Animated-Axe_Armor_(Ranged_Attack).gif","w":111,"h":120,"c":["Ranged attack animation"]}]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"external-links","title":"External links","blocks":[{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"Old Axe Armor","x":"https://castlevania.fandom.com/wiki/Old_Axe_Armor"}," on the ",{"t":" Castlevania Wiki","x":"https://castlevania.fandom.com/"}]}]}],"subs":[]}]}